			"id": "what-the-caveats-mean",
			"depth": 2,
			"text": "What the caveats mean"
		},
		{
			"id": "if-a-chip-is-not-listed",
			"depth": 2,
			"text": "If a chip is not listed"
		}
	],
	"body": [
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Fixture App talks to tags through Core NFC, so a chip only works if it answers as one of the tag types iOS exposes: Type 2 over ISO 14443A, Type 4 over ISO 7816, or Type 5 over ISO 15693. A chip that answers only on a proprietary protocol shows up as an identifier and nothing more."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Every result below came from an iPhone 13 and an iPhone 15 Pro running iOS 18.2, against blank tags from three suppliers. Read means the Scan sheet pulls the NDEF message off the tag with no extra setup. Write means the Write sheet puts a new message back and reports the free bytes left afterwards. User memory is the space an NDEF message can occupy, which is always less than the total memory on the die."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "table",
			"align": [
				null,
				null
			],
			"header": [
				{
					"type": "tableCell",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Estado"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "tableCell",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Significado"
						}
					]
				}
			],
			"rows": [
				[
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "status",
								"value": "yes"
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "Verificado en hardware. Fixture App lee y escribe todos los tipos de registro que admite el chip, incluidas las p\u00e1ginas NDEF bloqueadas."
							}
						]
					}
				],
				[
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "status",
								"value": "partial"
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "Parcial. La lectura funciona, la escritura no, normalmente porque el chip viene con una contrase\u00f1a del fabricante que Fixture App no puede establecer."
							}
						]
					}
				],
				[
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "status",
								"value": "no"
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "No compatible. El chip se reconoce durante el descubrimiento, y la sesi\u00f3n termina antes de cualquier escritura, as\u00ed que la etiqueta queda intacta."
							}
						]
					}
				],
				[
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "status",
								"value": "na"
							}
						]
					},
					{
						"type": "tableCell",
						"children": [
							{
								"type": "text",
								"value": "No aplicable. Este chip no tiene una superficie NDEF que Fixture App pueda usar."
							}
						]
					}
				]
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "El estado se registra por revisi\u00f3n del chip, as\u00ed que comprueba la revisi\u00f3n indicada en la fila en lugar del nombre de familia impreso en el envase."
				}
			]
		},
