		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "what-the-caveats-mean",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "What the caveats mean"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "A "
				},
				{
					"type": "status",
					"value": "partial"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " in the Write column means the chip accepts a write only after an extra step, never that the write is unreliable once it starts."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "NTAG424 DNA ships with its NDEF file locked behind AES authentication, so the Write sheet asks for the application key before it will change anything. Ultralight C uses 3DES on the pages above the counter, and Fixture App writes below the lock byte unless you paste the key into Settings, Advanced, Tag keys. ICODE SLIX2 answers on ISO 15693 and stores its message in blocks of four bytes, so the free-byte figure drops in steps of four."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "DESFire EV3 is readable and no more. The phone can select the NDEF application and read what is in it, but creating or resizing the file needs a key we will not ask you to carry, so the write button stays dim and shows \"This tag is read only on iPhone\". MIFARE Classic 1K is not readable at all. iOS hands back the identifier and stops there, and the Scan sheet reports error 2001, \"Tag is not NDEF compliant\". Neither chip has a figure in the memory column: on DESFire the size is fixed when the file is created, and on Classic there is no NDEF file to measure."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"id": "if-a-chip-is-not-listed",
			"idSource": "slug",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If a chip is not listed"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Send the tag identifier from the Scan sheet and the marking printed on the packaging to "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "mailto",
					"address": "docs@example.com",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "docs@example.com"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and we will test it. A chip on this list can still fail behind a case with a metal plate or a payment card, which is covered in "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"kind": "internal",
					"slug": "guide/troubleshooting",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "When a scan does not work"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		}
